.el .ds Aq '
.TH geectl-local-build-log 1  "geectl-local-build-log 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-local\-build\-log \- Read the log of the last local build: the `<root>/.build.log` the build\*(Aqs coordinates name. A read: no `\-\-live` needed. The text is the log verbatim (design rule 4); the verdict, exit code, log path, and truncation flag ride in the JSON payload
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl local\-build log\fR [\fB\-\-flavor\fR] [\fB\-\-tail\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-project\fR> <\fIREPO\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> <\fISPEC\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the log of the last local build: the `<root>/.build.log` the build\*(Aqs coordinates name. A read: no `\-\-live` needed. The text is the log verbatim (design rule 4); the verdict, exit code, log path, and truncation flag ride in the JSON payload
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project the package belongs to
.TP
\fB\-\-flavor\fR \fI<FLAVOR>\fR
The multibuild flavor; required when the source carries a `_multibuild` file
.TP
\fB\-\-tail\fR \fI<TAIL>\fR
Print only the last N lines of the log
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Read the whole log without the 4 MiB cap
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREPO\fR>
The repository the root was built for
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the root was built for
.TP
<\fISPEC\fR>
The source directory (spec + sources); the package comes from the spec file in it, like the build
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
